		about_f3 = "Free work camera (fly, orbit, pan, wheel zoom) and scene cameras you can look through, aim at objects and match to the work view.",
		about_f4 = "Posing: move, rotate and scale objects and single bones with a gizmo in world or local space, with snapping; inverse kinematics for arms and legs; copy and paste poses between models with the same skeleton.",
		about_f5 = "Every bone can be posed: bones without a physics body — clavicles, shoulders, fingers on many characters — are moved, rotated and scaled too. Bone markers are small so they do not hide the fingers; their size is set in View → Bone size.",
