		shader_pack_empty = "no materials or compiled shaders (.vmt, .vcs) found",
		shader_pack_lua_only = "Lua only: install this addon into garrysmod/addons and use Engine frame",
		shader_pack_big = "the pack is too large (over 256 MB)",
		shader_pack_mount = "the game could not mount the pack",
		shader_pack_error = "error while reading the pack (see console)",
		fxc_custom = "Custom shaders (Workshop, addons, shader folder)",
		fx_shader = "Custom shader %d",
		fx_shader_pick = "choose a shader material…",
		fx_shader_none = "No shader materials found. Install a shader addon or put a pack into the shader folder (Windows → Addon shaders → Shader folder).",
		fx_shader_missing = "Shader material not found: %s",
		fx_shader_buffers = "This shader reads engine buffers (depth, normals). They exist only for the game's main frame, so use it together with Engine frame.",
		about_f1 = "SFM-like workspace: windows dock side by side, tabs can be dragged out, layouts are saved and restored. Any window can be kept above the others: right-click its tab bar → Window properties → Always on top (the Model Browser is on top by default).",
		about_f2 = "Primary and Secondary viewports with an aspect gate, composition guides (thirds, golden ratio, centre, safe areas) and a fixed exposure.",
		about_f11 = "Lights: point and spot lights with colour, range and brightness, ready-made presets and a three-point rig around the selected model. Spot lights have soft shadows with their own edge softness, depth and slope bias and near plane, adjustable falloff, a parallel sun-like beam and light masks.",
		about_f12 = "Shadows tab: shadow map quality, how many lights cast shadows and up to what distance from the camera, a global softness multiplier; prop shadows from map lighting — on or off, detailed or blobs, how many are drawn, their length, colour and direction.",
		about_f13 = "Camera effects for scene cameras (the work camera has none): fisheye, vignette, tone curves for RGB and each channel, HDR, bloom, sharpen, sobel, toy town, texturize, material overlay and up to three custom shaders. They are set in the Render window and show in its preview and in the final render; the viewports stay clean.",
		about_f14 = "Shaders from the Workshop and addons. Engine frame mode lets the game's own renderer draw the picture, so post-processing addons — including shaders built on GShader Library — get into the preview and the final render. The Addon shaders window lists every registered effect with its own settings panel.",
		about_f15 = "Shader folder: put a downloaded shader pack (materials and shaders/fxc) into addons/speditor/shaders and press Rescan — it is mounted without restarting the game and its shaders appear in the Custom shader list.",
		about_f16 = "Multi-selection (Shift or Ctrl + click): move, rotate, scale, duplicate and delete several objects at once.",
		about_f17 = "Pose library and scenes: save, load, autosave with several backups; scenes keep the camera, the frame settings, object properties, light settings and camera effects.",
		about_f18 = "Render to PNG or JPEG up to 3840 px off-screen: anti-aliasing, depth of field, fullbright and a large live preview that scales with the Render window.",
		about_f19 = "Undo and redo for every edit.",
		about_f20 = "Editor notifications: saves, autosaves, renders, errors and hints appear as cards in the corner of the screen, in the style of the interface. The message log, sound and display time are in Windows → Notifications.",
		about_f21 = "Interface themes: GM:FM UI, a copy of the standard GMod skin, bundled skins and your own from the themes folder. The editor uses only its own skins, so interface addons from the Workshop do not break it; changing the theme keeps fullbright, open windows and the selected camera.",
