		nse_where = "Saved to garrysmod/data/speditor/notify_styles/<name>.json. To share a style in a Workshop addon, put the file into data_static/speditor/notify_styles/; a lua file in lua/speditor_notify/ can draw a style completely (SPeditor.UI.AddNotifyStyle).",
		-- About: list of changes of the current version
		about_news = "New in %s",
		about_n1 = "GM:FM UI is now the look of Source Filmmaker's own Qt interface: its colours, buttons, fields, check boxes, tabbed windows, menus, transport and gizmo buttons and item icons (taken from SFM's style sheets and pictures). The earlier look is the theme SPeditor UI (b0.1).",
		about_n2 = "The Motion Editor's procedural presets, SFM's whole list: 19 presets in groups (Smooth, Sharp, Steady, Jitter, Hold, Round, Default, Stagger; In, Out, Ramp, Spline, Drop, Release; Zero, Half, One; Playhead, Paste) over the keys inside the time selection. Falloff shapes Ease in and Ease out, and Autofalloff to bookmarks.",
		about_n3 = "Timeline bookmarks (the flag button; drag, rename, saved with the scene) and play modes: once, loop, to the end and back (bounce).",
		about_n4 = "Point and orient constraints (Attach to… → an object): follow only the place or only the turn of another object or of a ragdoll's bone. A rotator (endless turning in Procedural motion), Detach keeping the motion, the shot list exported as text.",
		about_n5 = "Environment window (Windows → Environment): the sun with cascaded shadows over the whole map, the brightness of the map's baked light, the map's baked sun turned off, any skybox or the painted sky, fog. Saved with the scene; one button puts the map back.",
		about_n6 = "FX clips on the timeline, as in SFM: titles and captions, film grain, colour correction and a material over the frame on a stretch of the film, with fades in and out.",
		about_n7 = "Ambient occlusion of Source Filmmaker itself (its shader rebuilt for GMod), and progressive like SFM's render: SSAO passes are averaged, the finished frame has no noise.",
		about_n8 = "Volumetric light: a spot light's beam is seen in the air, with the pattern of its mask and the shadows of what stands in it.",
		about_n9 = "Light masks picked from pictures; a selection box in the viewport and in the object list, Ctrl + A; every selected object is highlighted in the Animation Set Editor.",
		about_n10 = "Secondary Viewport refresh setting; particle effects play whole on the timeline; the player in the look of Windows Media Player; grey SFM glyphs on the tool buttons.",
		about_n11 = "Fixed: an error of some interface themes (dproperties.lua: bad argument #3 to SetDrawColor) when editing in the Element Viewer.",
